{"name":"Falcon Grey","hex":"#898887","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"falcon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any bird of the genus Falco, all of which are birds of prey.","Any bird of prey of the subfamilies Falconinae and Herpetotherinae."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt with a falcon or falcons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/falcon"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Falcon","blocks":[{"text":"Falcons are birds of prey in the genus Falco, which includes about 40 species. Some small species of falcons with long, narrow wings are called hobbies, and some that hover while hunting are called kestrels. Falcons are widely distributed on all continents of the world except Antarctica, though closely related raptors did occur there in the Eocene."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Eurasian_hobby_%28Falco_subbuteo%29_by_Shantanu_Kuveskar.jpg/330px-Eurasian_hobby_%28Falco_subbuteo%29_by_Shantanu_Kuveskar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falcon"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/